  "description": "A model fragment: any subset of the model's top-level member arrays, composed into the model root by `fragments[]`. PACK-12 (2026-08-17): this file previously declared 14 keys and NOT `concepts`, while setting additionalProperties:false -- so as written it rejected the most ordinary fragment there is. It had no consumer, which is exactly why it could be wrong unnoticed; `resolve_split_model` now validates every fragment file against it. The property list is generated from the composer's own key set (npdev_cli.MODEL_ARRAY_KEYS) rather than typed, because typing it is how it went stale.",
